  "guide.dns.cloudflareRecordFigure": "Cloudflare, DNS, Add record: an A record left DNS only (grey cloud).",
  "guide.dns.dnsOnly": "DNS only (recommended): the A records point straight at the server. Everything works, including Chat's real-time connection and every subdomain.",
  "guide.dns.figure": "The records to add, with your values.",
  "guide.dns.flexible": "Avoid Flexible: Cloudflare then cuts Chat's real-time connection, so chats never sync. If the zone must stay on Flexible, add a Configuration Rule that sets SSL to Full (strict) for chat.<domain>.",
  "guide.dns.keepTxt": "Keep the TXT record after the claim: the server checks it every 6 hours, and a domain that fails 3 checks in a row is suspended until DNS is right again.",
  "guide.dns.proxied": "Proxied through Cloudflare (orange cloud) also works, with the zone's SSL mode on Full (strict). The server has a real certificate for these hosts.",
  "guide.dns.sslModeFigure": "Cloudflare, SSL/TLS: for proxied hosts pick Full (Strict) and save, not Flexible.",
  "guide.dns.title": "2. Add the DNS records",
  "guide.dns.wildcard": "*.localman. and *.tunnel. are two-level wildcards: Cloudflare's free plan has no edge certificate for them. Keep them DNS only unless you pay for one.",
  "guide.figure": "Figure {number}.",
  "guide.intro": "Once set up, your users sign in at auth.<domain> and use Chat at chat.<domain>, Localman at localman.<domain> and Tunelo at tunnel.<domain>. Nothing to install: everything runs on hoandat.com's servers. Accounts, sessions, projects and tunnels of your domain never mix with another domain's.",
  "guide.keep.body": "The domain stays yours while the TXT record stays and the records point at the server. To remove it, delete the TXT record or ask the operator: its certificates, token and all its data are deleted, and the domain can be claimed again.",
  "guide.keep.title": "Keeping or removing the domain",
  "guide.prepare.account": "An account at auth.hoandat.com with Google or GitHub linked. That Google or GitHub identity becomes the owner of the domain.",
  "guide.prepare.cloudflare": "Recommended: DNS on Cloudflare, with an API token (step 6). Without it, mocks and tunnels on subdomains cannot get a certificate.",
  "guide.prepare.dns": "Access to your domain's DNS. A subdomain of a domain you own (dev.example.com) works too.",
  "guide.prepare.oauth": "A Google Cloud or GitHub account, to create the sign-in app of your domain (step 5).",
  "guide.prepare.title": "Before you start",
  "guide.self.apps": "Your own Google or GitHub sign-in app, and a Cloudflare Turnstile widget for localman.<domain>.",
  "guide.self.body": "When {claim} offers it, choose On your own servers in step 1. You only add the TXT record; the hosts point at your server, not here. Once the domain is verified, download the setup bundle (valid for 24 hours) and follow {installGuide}. Your server then completes the setup with Auth Next once, and nothing goes through hoandat.com afterwards.",
  "guide.self.cloudflare": "DNS on Cloudflare with an API token that edits the zone: the wildcard certificates of *.localman. and *.tunnel. are proven through DNS.",
  "guide.self.duty": "Auth Next does not back up, update, patch or watch your server: that is up to you. Keep the TXT record so nobody else can claim the domain here.",
  "guide.self.installGuide": "the install guide",
  "guide.self.move": "Moving a domain that already runs here: in Your domains, press Move to your own servers. The domain stops being served here at once, its data kept; Cancel the move serves it again. Install the bundle without pointing the A records at your server yet, and send the operator your install's migration public key. The operator exports the domain's accounts, projects, variables, tunnel keys and messages for your server only; import them there, then point the A records at it. Tokens already issued keep working; people sign in to Localman and Chat again once.",
  "guide.self.server": "A Linux server with Docker Compose, a public IPv4, ports 80 and 443 and Tunelo's TCP ports open, and about 4 GB of free memory.",
  "guide.self.title": "Running the domain on your own server",
  "guide.signin.body": "Your users sign in with a Google or GitHub app that belongs to your domain. One is enough; add both if you like.",
  "guide.signin.github": "GitHub: Settings, Developer settings, OAuth Apps, New OAuth App. Homepage URL https://auth.<domain>, redirect URI https://auth.<domain>/oauth/github/callback. Then generate a client secret.",
  "guide.signin.githubFigure": "GitHub, Register a new OAuth app: homepage and redirect URI.",
  "guide.signin.googleBranding": "Google: in Google Cloud, open Google Auth Platform, Branding. Fill the home page https://auth.<domain>, the privacy policy https://auth.<domain>/privacy (the page exists already) and add your domain as an authorized domain.",
  "guide.signin.googleBrandingFigure": "Google Auth Platform, Branding: home page, privacy policy and authorized domain.",
  "guide.signin.googleClient": "Then Clients, Create client: type Web application, authorized redirect URI https://auth.<domain>/oauth/google/callback.",
  "guide.signin.googleClientFigure": "Create OAuth client ID: Web application and its redirect URI.",
  "guide.signin.paste": "Paste the client ID and client secret into the admin page and save. The domain is active as soon as one provider is saved. Secrets are never shown again, and the last provider cannot be removed.",
  "guide.signin.pasteFigure": "The admin page shows the exact callback URL to register.",
  "guide.signin.title": "5. Add Google or GitHub sign-in",
  "guide.subtitle": "Run sign-in, Chat, Localman and Tunelo on a domain you own, with their own accounts.",
  "guide.title": "Use your own domain",
  "guide.token.body": "Mocks (<secret>.localman.<domain>) and tunnels (<name>.tunnel.<domain>) need a wildcard certificate, proved through DNS. At dash.cloudflare.com: My Profile, API Tokens, Create Token, template Edit zone DNS, zone of your domain. Paste it into the admin page; it is checked by creating and deleting a TXT record, then sealed for the certificate service.",
  "guide.token.createFigure": "Zone DNS Edit, limited to your domain under Zone Resources.",
  "guide.token.figure": "Where the Cloudflare token goes.",
  "guide.token.templateFigure": "Cloudflare, API Tokens, Create Token: use the Edit zone DNS template.",
  "guide.token.title": "6. Cloudflare token (DNS on Cloudflare)",
  "guide.token.without": "Without a token the main pages still work; mocks and tunnels on subdomains do not.",
  "guide.users.accounts": "Accounts: https://auth.<domain>. They are separate from hoandat.com accounts, even for the same person.",
  "guide.users.chat": "Chat: https://chat.<domain>.",
  "guide.users.localman": "Localman: https://localman.<domain>; mocks at https://<secret>.localman.<domain>; MCP at https://localman.<domain>/mcp.",
  "guide.users.scribe": "Scribe (transcription, meeting notes), once you add an AI key in the Scribe section of admin, where this server offers it: https://scribe.<domain>.",
  "guide.users.title": "7. Your users",
  "guide.users.tunelo": "Tunelo: CLI 1.8.0 or later (npm install -g tunelo@latest), then tunelo login --server https://tunnel.<domain>.",
  "guide.verify.body": "Wait a few minutes for DNS to spread, then press Check DNS. Records that do not point at the server yet are marked; fix them and check again.",
  "guide.verify.done": "When every record is right the domain is yours and its certificates are issued within minutes. It appears under Your domains.",
  "guide.verify.doneFigure": "The claimed domain, ready for its admin page.",
  "guide.verify.title": "3. Check DNS",
  "guide.verify.wrongFigure": "One record not right yet: chat.<domain> is marked.",
